  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc / 46.4% F1, while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 20.8% acc. RNA is clearly the dominant modality, so improving its representation is the highest-priority question. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether a learned, domain-specific encoder (scvi_n200) can outperform a simple linear PCA projection, or whether PCA already captures the relevant signal. This experiment (config_004) is a clean single-variable change from config_001—only the RNA encoder changes (pca_n2000 → scvi_n200), keeping singleprofile and no aggregation/fusion—so any performance difference can be attributed to the representation choice. If scvi substantially beats PCA, it justifies investing further in learned encoders and multimodal fusion with a stronger RNA backbone; if it does not, it tells us PCA is sufficient and we should redirect budget toward profile settings, image encoders, or fusion strategies. Under the limited budget, isolating the representation effect on our strongest modality is the most informative next step before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

